{"id": "EUVD-2026-103732", "enisaUuid": "4cb58ce5-dc08-380c-8375-5c7a8ae52483", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet: macb: fix dma_alloc_coherent() leak on macb_alloc() error paths\n\nFix 3 leaks in macb_alloc() error paths:\n- Tx buffer allocated but crossing a 4G boundary: Tx leaked.\n- Rx buffer allocation fails: Tx leaked.\n- Rx buffer allocated but crossing a 4G boundary: Tx & Rx leaked.\n\nThis is because our error handling calls macb_free(bp) which in turn\nfrees the buffers stored in bp->queues[0], but nothing has been stored\nin there. Fix by storing allocated buffers into bp->queues[0] ASAP.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:16:21", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:20:29", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bda487567d0b7b15dfa876511085c0666b9efad5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/259e6cbb6a097da8ced544ee92a6fbde35aa1338", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/23d42b9a3bcd55b17d3b371544fedc708c2397e9"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98492", "GHSA-pvj4-6qwf-8pwq"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1da9a395-80da-3223-880c-4be06bb0373e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "78d901897b3cae06b38f54e48a2378cf9da21175 <23d42b9a3bcd55b17d3b371544fedc708c2397e9"}, {"id": "3cca87c4-ef29-38fb-bd80-890e28fb552c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.9"}, {"id": "6d2205ab-23c3-3e08-a421-2ab11bfdc9fb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.55"}, {"id": "6e691785-6ddd-3296-83d9-439f63d0f4b4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "78d901897b3cae06b38f54e48a2378cf9da21175 <259e6cbb6a097da8ced544ee92a6fbde35aa1338"}, {"id": "77a57024-39e5-3a3c-8351-b88157ba93d8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.18"}, {"id": "82b1652b-b8da-3c14-9a97-41c877f6c2d